(324+121+64+16+36+9) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 570 \\\\  & =\\frac{570}{6} \\\\  & =95.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =95-{(-5)}^{2} \\\\  & =95-25 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359413 13194139535656 true] [17592186359412 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535656 true] [17592186359412 1041 "field-1" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359412 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359413 13194139535656 true] [17592186359412 1110 #uuid "56179feb-ba3d-5788-94a3-2da70f22fed1" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359413 1034 "70" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535656 true] [17592186359413 1111 #uuid "0e34cd32-bdd9-5982-92d6-d8c373fb531a" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359414 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359415 13194139535656 true] [17592186359414 1089 "q-263451" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359414 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535656 true] [17592186359414 1100 "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n10,\\,14,\\,16,\\,9,\\,12,\\,5\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359414 1113 #uuid "0b72f295-29a5-54b1-8266-2fadea925b1a" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359414 1145 "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (10+14+16+9+12+5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 66 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot [{10}^{2}+{14}^{2}+{16}^{2}+{9}^{2}+{12}^{2}+{5}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot [100+196+256+81+144+25] \\\\  & =\\frac{802}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}-{(11)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}-121 \\\\  & =\\frac{401-363}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{38}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359416 13194139535656 true] [17592186359415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359417 13194139535656 true] [17592186359415 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535656 true] [17592186359415 1041 "field-1" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359415 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359416 13194139535656 true] [17592186359415 1110 #uuid "efbe38a0-c7c6-5108-b180-f56d2527b1d5" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359416 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{38}{3}}" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535656 true] [17592186359416 1111 #uuid "e61e7f97-98d1-5e60-b965-3c4b6b96c7b2" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359417 1034 "\\frac{38}{3}" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535656 true] [17592186359417 1111 #uuid "d968abf2-e650-585c-9021-6d98031f7510" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359418 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359419 13194139535656 true] [17592186359418 1089 "q-263584" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359418 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535656 true] [17592186359418 1100 "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n9,\\,4,\\,15,\\,14,\\,18,\\,7,\\,17\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535656 true] [17592186359418 1113 #uuid "d8be7b4